---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import delta from "../../images/projects/australia-2024-qualifying-delta.png";
import turnThree from "../../images/projects/australia-2024-turn-3.png";
import "../../styles/projects.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Formula 1 analysis · Nelson Jeanrenaud" description="A sample of my Python telemetry analysis: comparing Ocon and Gasly in qualifying at the 2024 Australian Grand Prix, with my original charts.">
  <SiteHeader />
  <span id="top"></span>
  <main class="wrap project-detail">
    <section class="section">
      <a class="project-detail__back" href="/#projects">Back to projects</a>
      <p class="kicker">Personal project · Python · 2021–2024</p>
      <h1>Formula 1 data analysis</h1>
      <p class="lead">Turning race telemetry into an explanation of where lap time is gained and lost.</p>
      <p>I built Python tooling for telemetry and session analysis and published race-weekend reports. Here I revisit my article “How Ocon got out of Q1”, which I published on 23 March 2024.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="question">
      <h2 id="question">The question</h2>
      <p>At the 2024 Australian Grand Prix, Ocon reached the second qualifying session while Gasly did not. I compared their laps to investigate where the difference emerged, using time-delta and corner-level telemetry charts.</p>
      <figure class="project-evidence">
        <a href={delta.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the qualifying time-delta chart at full size">
          <Image src={delta} alt="Time-delta chart comparing Ocon and Gasly across a qualifying lap at the 2024 Australian Grand Prix." width={1200} />
        </a>
        <figcaption>My original time-delta chart from the article. Open the image for a closer look.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="comparison">
      <h2 id="comparison">From lap time to driving behaviour</h2>
      <p>At turn three, I associated Ocon's later braking and greater corner-entry speed with a gain of about two tenths. I compared speed, throttle and brake traces to understand the drivers' approaches and what lay behind the final lap times.</p>
      <figure class="project-evidence">
        <a href={turnThree.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the turn-three telemetry chart at full size">
          <Image src={turnThree} alt="Original turn-three comparison chart showing Ocon and Gasly's telemetry and relative time difference." width={1200} loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <figcaption>My original corner-level chart for turn three.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h3>What I could not confirm</h3>
      <p>Public telemetry is incomplete. Brake-pedal pressure is unavailable, and recorded gear changes do not necessarily show attempted shifts. I could not establish the impact of Gasly's reported shifting problems from those traces. I could describe the recorded behaviour, but not recover every cause behind it.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="evidence">
      <h2 id="evidence">Read my articles</h2>
      <ul class="project-detail__sources">
        <li><a href="/blog/how-ocon-got-out-of-q1/">Read How Ocon got out of Q1</a></li>
        <li><a href="/blog/">Browse all my Formula 1 articles</a></li>
        <li><a href="/projects/pit-stop-modelling">Related academic work: pit-stop decision modelling</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
